cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Historical monetary data"
message: "If you use these datasets, please cite this collection and also the underlying primary sources listed in each dataset's README."
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Miguel
    family-names: González Calvo
    email: miguel.gc@me.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/MiguelPuntoEs/historical-monetary-data"
url: "https://www.miguel.es/data"
abstract: >-
  Machine-readable transcriptions of primary-source monetary data, taken from page
  images rather than optical character recognition. The collection currently holds
  the scales of depreciation enacted by seven American states to settle debts in
  Continental currency (1777-1781), with contemporary merchants' quotations for
  Philadelphia and Virginia; and prices, wages and the money stock during the
  American Civil War (1859-1866) from Wesley C. Mitchell. Where an enacted statute
  survives it is preferred to later reprints, and where printed compilations
  disagree both are published rather than one being silently chosen.
keywords:
  - monetary history
  - economic history
  - paper money
  - primary sources
  - Continental dollar
  - greenbacks
license: CC0-1.0
